# Build output. `build/` has no leading slash, so it matches the root project's and every
# module's, at any depth — including composeApp/build/outputs/mapping/, R8's symbol map, which
# is a build artifact even though RELEASING.md says to keep a copy of it.
build/
out/
captures/

# Gradle's and Kotlin's own caches. Machine-local and regenerated on demand.
.gradle/
.kotlin/
*.hprof

# Where the Android SDK lives on this machine. Every checkout has a different answer, which is
# why the build reads it from here rather than from a committed file.
local.properties

# Anything that could sign or publish a release. The directory rather than a pattern per file,
# so a secret added later is ignored before anyone has to remember to add it — and the keystore
# patterns as well, for a key someone drops outside it.
.secrets/
composeApp/keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# IDEs and editors. The Gradle build is the source of truth; nobody should need another
# checkout's project files to open this one.
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# The web target's toolchain. `kotlin-js-store/yarn.lock` is deliberately *not* here: it pins
# the Wasm build's npm dependencies and belongs in the repository.
node_modules/

# Scratch output from tools that run against the app — MCP browser sessions, the Python in
# play/ — none of which is part of the app.
.playwright-mcp/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# A symlink to an unrelated checkout on one machine, used as reference material. It would be
# committed as a dangling symlink for everyone else.
/example-app

# OS droppings.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
